{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966791,"nonce":"n4KbMFz3tSlRcVplVT7JKtyzx9Q=","title":"Desktop subtree rebuilds skip CSS class-only @keyframes animations on the first","message":"On desktop, the FIRST time a CSS class-only `@keyframes` animation is supposed to fire (popover / context-menu / dropdown / select / combobox / menubar open), the element snaps in instantly. The SECOND interaction and onwards plays the animation correctly. Web is unaffected — animations play every time.\n\nLikely cause: timing race between `process_pending_subtree_rebuilds` and `start_all_css_animations` in windowed.rs around line 5071. By the time `start_all_css_animations` walks `element_registry.class_to_nodes_index()`, either:\n- The class index hasn't yet been updated for the freshly-mounted overlay subtree, OR\n- `stable_id_or_warn` returns a stale id from the prior frame, OR\n- The animation entry from a previous mount is still in `css_anim_store` with `is_playing=false`, and the `already_has` guard skips re-firing it.\n\nThe web path goes through a different call site (web.rs:2511 after subtree rebuild) which appears to land at the right time.\n\n**Why:** The class-anim-start fix in commit 692243a1 added a class-iteration pass to `start_all_css_animations`, but the timing on desktop's subtree rebuild path means the freshly-mounted overlay isn't yet visible to the iteration on the first frame.\n\n**How to apply:** Test cn dropdown surfaces (context-menu, popover, dropdown, select, combobox, menubar) on desktop. If you see \"first open is instant, second open animates\", this is the known issue — don't spend time debugging the keyframes / CSS. The fix is in the rebuild→class-index→start ordering, not in the animation itself.\n\nRecording references: `Screen Recording 2026-05-22*` (cn_demo demo session where this was observed).","files":null}]}